<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech July real ind. output rises 15.6 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Czech July real ind. output rises 15.6 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech real definitive industrial output in July grew by 15.6 percent compared with the same month in 1995, the Czech Statistical Bureau said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said average nominal monthly wages grew 19.7 percent in July compared with a 13.3 percent in June, year-on-year.  </p>
<p> INDUSTRIAL OUTPUT  JULY/96	JUNE/96  JAN-JULY 96 JULY/95</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr   +15.6 (+16.3)  +1.8    +9.1 (9.2)   +7.2</p>
<p> NOMINAL INDUSTRIAL MONTHLY WAGES</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr   +19.7 (+19.6) +13.3   +17.7 (17.8) +n/a</p>
<p>NOTE: Preliminary estimates in brackets. The average nominal industrial wage in July was 9,633 crowns compared with 9,636 in June. Wage results sample companies with 100 or more employees while output results include estimates of smaller firms as well.</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
